-- #1111 A-2.7 OVER-BINDING GUARD: `import m.{T(..)}` binds the constructors of
-- `T`, and no others of `m`.
--
-- The cheap way to make a `(..)` member bind something is to hand it every
-- constructor the exporting module has.  That is wrong, and this program is where
-- it shows: the import frame is scanned FIRST-match in source order, so an
-- over-binding `omodn.{OT(..)}` clause would put omodn's arity-1 `Wid` ahead of the
-- arity-2 `Wid` the next clause imports by name, and `Wid 1 2` would build a
-- partial application instead of a `PU`.
--
-- The clause ORDER is the trigger and must not be "tidied": omodn must be first.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand BEFORE any capture and independently of any
-- engine: `unOT (Zed 4)` = `4`; `unPU (Wid 1 2)` = `1 + 2` = `3`.  So `4` then `3`.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS FIXTURE IS GREEN ON PRISTINE `main` TOO, and that is stated rather than
-- hidden: before A-2.7 the `(..)` member bound nothing at all, so it could not
-- over-bind.  Its counterfactual is therefore a MUTATION of the fix, not a revert —
-- `memberCells`'s `(..)` arm made to bind `flatMap snd ctorsByType` (every
-- constructor of the exporting module) instead of the named type's.  MEASURED on a
-- binary built from that mutation: RED, `REGRESS
-- llvmM/ctor_scope_type_member_no_overbind`, eval `E-NOT-A-FUNCTION: applied
-- non-function: Wid 1` against a native arm still printing `4|3`.  The other two
-- A-2.7 fixtures stayed GREEN under the same mutation, so this is the only member
-- of the set that sees it.  Do not cite this fixture as evidence that A-2.7 changed
-- anything; cite it as the thing that fails if the next edit widens the rule.
--
-- IT IS ALSO THE SET'S BYSTANDER CELL.  The mechanism is present (`omodn.{OT(..)}`
-- builds an overlay) while the second assertion is about `pmodn`, a module the
-- mechanism must not reach — and unlike `ctor_scope_type_member_per_module/`, both
-- sides of the counterfactual are green, so "unrelated code still behaves" is
-- observable here rather than inferred.
--
-- ⚠️ IT DOES NOT COVER THE WHOLE OVER-BINDING FAMILY, and A-2.7 shipped a second
-- member of that family past this fixture.  What this one detects is binding the
-- WRONG TYPE'S constructors from the right module.  It is blind to binding the
-- RIGHT type's constructor from a decl the exporting module does not EXPORT —
-- `test/eval_modules_fixtures/ctor_type_member_newtype_not_bound/` is the cell for
-- that, and it went red on a cut this fixture passed.  Over-binding is a family:
-- "which decl?" and "will the front end bind it at all?" are separate gates and need
-- separate cells.  (That cell lives in the interpreter-only corpus on purpose — the
-- native arm is wrong on its shape today, #1305 — so it is not a sibling directory
-- here and the path is spelled in full.)
import omodn.{OT(..), unOT}
import pmodn.{PU, Wid, unPU}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (intToString (unOT (Zed 4)))
  putStrLn (intToString (unPU (Wid 1 2)))
